From: Kitsune <kitsune@akitsune.dev>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 20:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: Validate rendering mode when reusing glyph bitmaps

Wine's per-font-face cache identifies glyph data by font size, glyph index,
and measuring mode. Bitmap layout also depends on rendering mode, however.
Aliased and antialiased rendering can produce different pitches and buffer
sizes for the same cache key. Reusing an entry from another rendering mode
can therefore copy a cached bitmap into a smaller destination and corrupt the
heap.

Record the rendering mode used for a cached bitmap and reuse bitmap data only
when both its rendering mode and exact size match. Render mismatched modes
directly, and do not mark a bitmap as cached when its allocation fails.

TouchDesigner renders the same font faces, glyphs, and sizes through multiple
rendering modes while constructing its UI font atlases. This exposed the bad
cache reuse as splash-screen hangs and heap-corruption crashes in palette text
operators. Keeping rendering mode as part of the cached bitmap state prevents
the incompatible copy without adding any TouchDesigner-specific behavior.

---
 dlls/dwrite/font.c | 24 ++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/dwrite/font.c b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
index 3baa8d2d..b742d893 100644
--- a/dlls/dwrite/font.c
+++ b/dlls/dwrite/font.c
@@ -60,6 +60,7 @@ struct cache_entry
     RECT bbox;
     BYTE *bitmap;
     unsigned int bitmap_size;
+    DWRITE_RENDERING_MODE1 bitmap_mode;
     unsigned int is_1bpp : 1;
     unsigned int has_contours : 1;
     unsigned int has_advance : 1;
@@ -225,22 +226,33 @@ static HRESULT dwrite_fontface_get_glyph_bitmap(struct dwrite_fontface *fontface
     }
     else if ((entry = fontface_get_cache_entry(fontface, bitmap_size, &key)))
     {
-        if (entry->has_bitmap)
+        if (entry->has_bitmap && entry->bitmap_mode == rendering_mode && entry->bitmap_size == bitmap_size)
         {
             memcpy(bitmap->buf, entry->bitmap, entry->bitmap_size);
+            *is_1bpp = entry->is_1bpp;
+        }
+        else if (entry->has_bitmap)
+        {
+            /* Bbox and advance entries share this key, but bitmap layout also
+             * depends on rendering mode. Render a mismatched mode directly
+             * instead of copying a differently sized cached buffer. */
+            UNIX_CALL(get_glyph_bitmap, &params);
         }
         else
         {
             params.is_1bpp = &_1bpp;
             UNIX_CALL(get_glyph_bitmap, &params);

-            entry->bitmap_size = bitmap_size;
-            if ((entry->bitmap = malloc(entry->bitmap_size)))
+            if ((entry->bitmap = malloc(bitmap_size)))
+            {
+                entry->bitmap_size = bitmap_size;
+                entry->bitmap_mode = rendering_mode;
                 memcpy(entry->bitmap, bitmap->buf, entry->bitmap_size);
-            entry->is_1bpp = !!_1bpp;
-            entry->has_bitmap = 1;
+                entry->is_1bpp = !!_1bpp;
+                entry->has_bitmap = 1;
+            }
+            *is_1bpp = _1bpp;
         }
-        *is_1bpp = entry->is_1bpp;
     }
     else
         hr = E_FAIL;
